% ============================================================================
% cloud-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the cloud-altitude library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what level is a cirrus
% cloud?": it states no weather fact — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `cloud_altitude` rows and returns the level + the table's source/locator/
% trust. A cloud (or non-cloud) the NWS page never classifies abstains honestly
% — the engine never invents a level.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli cloud-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "cloud-types.adj"

? cloud_altitude(cirrus, $Level)        % expect high
? cloud_altitude(cumulus, $Level)       % expect low
? cloud_altitude(fog, $Level)           % expect abstain — the page never gives fog a level
